<%- include('../partials/plain-start', { title: 'Terms of use' }) %>
<article class="card prose">
  <h1>Terms of use</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated October 2026</p>

  <p>
    <%= appName %> is a student project built to practise secure authentication in Node.js.
    It isn't a commercial service, so please don't store anything here you'd mind losing.
  </p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Use an email address you can access. Your account stays inactive until you click the verification link.</li>
    <li>Pick a password you don't use anywhere else. It's stored only as a bcrypt hash, so nobody (including the admin) can read it.</li>
    <li>After several wrong passwords in a row the account is locked for a short time to slow down guessing.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What gets stored</h2>
  <p>
    Your name, email, a hash of your password, and a log of sign-in attempts (time, IP address and browser)
    so you can spot activity you don't recognise. Deleting your account from the settings page removes all of it.
  </p>

  <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>Don't try to break into other people's accounts or overload the service. Admins can deactivate accounts that do.</p>
</article>
<%- include('../partials/plain-end') %>
